On the shell, yoyo docs, yoyo risk <bad> and yoyo memories now print the yoyo <verb> form instead of telling you to type a slash command. The REPL text is unchanged and so are the exit codes. Build, the full cargo test, clippy with -D warnings and fmt --check all pass. Committed as fd971f51 under "Part of #1127".

Before → after (built binary, empty temp dir, fresh HOME, </dev/null):
• yoyo docs: usage: /docs <crate> [item] → usage: yoyo docs <crate> [item]. The examples line now reads Examples: yoyo docs serde, yoyo docs tokio task.
• yoyo risk zz1: Unknown /risk subcommand: zz1 → Unknown yoyo risk subcommand: zz1
• yoyo memories with no memories: Use /remember <note> to add one. → Add one in the REPL: run yoyo, then /remember <note>.

How:
• Each of the three handlers now takes a DoctorSurface and builds its message through the existing command_form. The REPL caller in dispatch.rs passes Repl; the shell caller in dispatch_sub.rs passes Shell.
• /remember and /forget have no shell command, so the shell hint says they are REPL commands rather than printing a yoyo remember that doesn't exist. A test checks there is still no such command and will fail if one is added, so the hint can name it then.
• The /forget <n> line printed under a memory listing comes from the same function and shows up on the shell too, so I fixed it the same way. That's slightly beyond the three lines the task named.

Tests:
• A new file, src/shell_form_tests.rs, checks both the shell and REPL text for all three messages. I put it in its own file so none of the size-capped files grew for tests.
• Two integration tests in tests/integration.rs asserted the old wrong text (Unknown /risk and usage: /docs). They now assert the shell form, and the docs one also checks that no /docs appears.

Size gate:
• commands_risk.rs went from 6615 to 6624 lines (+9 from this change).
• commands_project.rs went from 3709 to 3790: +10 from this change, the other 71 were already there before I started.
• I updated both entries in tests/module_size.rs with a reason.

